From: valix <djvalic.wc@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] motion_queuing: raise homing drip buffer to 300 ms

During homing and probing the host sends steps to the MCU in 50 ms
segments and keeps only DRIP_TIME (100 ms) queued ahead of the MCU
clock. On the AD5X the host can stall for up to ~0.3 s (seen right
after a large G-code upload), which empties the MCU step queue and
shuts down with "Timer too close".

Kiln OS: keep 300 ms queued instead. The MCU still stops on the trsync
trigger and drops later steps, so there is no overshoot; the cost is
about 0.2 s more wait after each homing or probe trigger. Issue #40.
---
--- a/klippy/extras/motion_queuing.py
+++ b/klippy/extras/motion_queuing.py
@@ -18,7 +18,8 @@
 SDS_CHECK_TIME = 0.001 # step+dir+step filter in stepcompress.c
 
 DRIP_SEGMENT_TIME = 0.050
-DRIP_TIME = 0.100
+# AD5X: the host can stall up to ~0.3 s after a large upload (issue #40)
+DRIP_TIME = 0.300
 
 class PrinterMotionQueuing:
     def __init__(self, config):
